{title: Lift Every Voice and Sing}
{artist: James Weldon Johnson / J. Rosamond Johnson}
{genre: Hymn, Gospel}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 60}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 519)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Lift every [G]voice and [Em]sing,
[Em]Till earth and [G]Heav[B7]en [Em]ring,
[Em]Ring with the [Am]har[B]mo[C]nies of [G]lib__[D7]__erty;
[D7]Let our re[G]joicing [E7]rise,
[E7]High as the [Am]lis[B]tening [C]skies,
[C]Let it re[G]sound [D7]loud as the rolling [G]sea.
[G]Sing a [E7]song full of the faith
[E7]That the dark past has [D]taught us,
[G]Sing a [Eb]song full of the hope
[Eb]That the present has [G]brought [D7]us;
[D7]Facing the [G]rising [E7]sun
[E7]Of our [Am]new day be[C]gun,
[C]Let us march [G]on [D7]till victory is [G]won.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Stony the [G]road we [Em]trod,
[Em]Bitter the [G]chast[B7]ening [Em]rod,
[Em]Felt in the [Am]days [B]when [C]hope un[G]born__[D7]__ had died;
[D7]Yet with a [G]steady [E7]beat,
[E7]Have not our [Am]wear[B]y [C]feet,
[C]Come to the [G]place [D7]for which our fathers [G]sighed?
[G]We have [E7]come over a way
[E7]That with tears has been [D]watered,
[G]We have [Eb]come, treading our path
[Eb]Through the blood of the [G]slaugh[D7]tered;
[D7]Out from the [G]gloomy [E7]past,
[E7]Till now [Am]we stand at [C]last
[C]Where the white [G]gleam [D7]of our bright star is [G]cast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]God of our [G]weary [Em]years,
[Em]God of our [G]si[B7]lent [Em]tears,
[Em]Thou who hast [Am]brought [B]us [C]thus far [G]on__[D7]__ the way;
[D7]Thou who hast [G]by Thy [E7]might,
[E7]Led us in[Am]to [B]the [C]light,
[C]Keep us for[G]ev[D7]er in the path, we [G]pray.
[G]Lest our [E7]feet stray from the places,
[E7]Our God, where we [D]met Thee.
[G]Lest our [Eb]hearts, drunk with the wine
[Eb]Of the world, we for[G]get [D7]Thee.
[D7]Shadowed be[G]neath Thy [E7]hand,
[E7]May we [Am]forever [C]stand,
[C]True to our [G]God, [D7]true to our native [G]land.
{end_of_verse}
